All this confusion over what fluency is is why I support the ILR
descriptors. Level 5 is the highest, but most native speakers are no more
than 3 or 3+.
And since I already said that 'native' implies 'fluent' (to me), then
'fluent' is 3 or higher, maybe even 2 or higher.

stevo

